codex
The pinned source corrects an important part of the copy hypothesis: prefill uploads the union of selected experts, grouping adjacent IDs into copies; it does not always upload all 256. The destination tensor still reserves space for all experts. Normal one-token decode falls below the default offload threshold and computes those matmuls on CPU.

I also confirmed that `-ot` and `--n-cpu-moe` place whole tensors or layers. They cannot place individual hot expert IDs, so I’ll record that limitation rather than propose a misleading static-placement run.

