+python3 review_results.py "$F19_RESULTS" # after run 6; writes review.json
+```
+
+`review.json` reports `passed_this_workload_screen` only if greedy output/prompt/host/image match, replay prompt drift <=10%, replay decode drift <=5%, candidate prompt gain >=10%, candidate decode change <=5%. Otherwise `reject_or_inconclusive`; no automatic deployment. A single bracketed screen is not a statistical claim across workloads. Cold preparation must leave <=1% model residency; summarize_model rejects failed engine/watchdog/cache/fill initialization/early-EOS runs. Each run uses a new output directory and refuses to overwrite one; set a new F19_RESULTS to repeat an approved experiment. Policy refusal may leave a diagnostic-only directory with no engine result.
