+B=$($Q submit --class build --name F19-build --timeout 3600 -- ./run_build.sh)
+$Q wait "$B" --timeout 3600
+```
+
+Preparation expected runtime **15-40 min** first time, <2 min incremental; outputs `build-operator/bin/expert-crossover`, `build-operator/probe_uma`, `build-operator.log`, `build-manifest.json`, final line `BUILD_OK`. Requires host cmake/C++/CUDA 12.6 compiler and the engine image's compatible CUDA runtime. The probe and harness run **inside the engine image**, using `sg docker -c "docker run --rm --runtime nvidia ..."`; model and placement mounts are read-only, only their fresh output directory is writable. The model workloads use the lab's `cc/om_run/om_run.sh` with per-file cold cache preparation, resource sampling, and its memory watchdog. Logs and results are all under F19_RESULTS. Before comparing, inspect clocks/temperature in telemetry; no clock or power-mode changes are made by these scripts.
+
+| Order (max 6 GPU jobs) | Command after previous job finishes | Runtime estimate / queue timeout | Expected output and information |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | `$Q submit --class gpu --name F19-base --timeout 900 -- ./run_model.sh baseline` | 2-6 min /900 s | `01-baseline/summary.json`: separate prompt_ms, decode_ms_per_token, decode_runs=63, prompt_tokens, stdout hash, decode fill bytes/wait. Common lab stdout/stderr/telemetry/cache records. Establish untraced threshold-32 baseline. |
